# Performance is a top priority for this site

The user has explicitly called this out as one of the most important things about
the product. Apply these defaults proactively — don't wait to be asked for a perf
pass after shipping a feature.

## D1 queries

- **Never query per-row in a loop.** If you need related rows (chapters, i18n, etc.)
  for N parent rows, fetch them in one batched query and group in JS (see
  `fetchChaptersForAllRoutines` in `lib/server/catalog/d1-repository.ts`), not one
  query per parent row. This bit us at `/api/v1/routines` (100 routines → 101
  queries → 9-13s) and `/api/v1/me/library` (one `getRoutine()` per purchase).
- **Add indexes** for any column used in a `WHERE`/`JOIN` on a table that can grow
  (see `migrations/0009_catalog_indexes.sql`). Ship them as new additive
  migrations — never edit an already-applied migration.
- **Dedupe per-request work.** If `generateMetadata` and the page body both need the
  same catalog/DB lookup, wrap it with React's `cache()` (see
  `getCachedRoutine`/`getCachedInstructor` in `lib/server/catalog/index.ts`) so it
  runs once per request instead of twice.

## Images / generated media

- `next.config.mjs` sets `images.unoptimized: true` (Cloudflare Workers can't run
  the sharp-based optimizer) — **nothing resizes or compresses images at runtime.**
  Whatever file is committed to `public/` is exactly what ships to the browser.
- **Never commit AI-generated images at their raw output resolution.** Resize +
  recompress before committing: instructor-style avatars → ~320×320 JPEG q≈80
  (~15-20KB), card/poster images → ~960×640 (~100-350KB). Use `sharp` (devDependency)
  — see `scripts/compress-generated-media.mjs` for the pattern. A single
  full-resolution generated avatar was 1.2-1.6MB vs ~15KB properly sized; across 18
  instructors that's 21MB vs 260KB for one page.
- For `next/image` with `fill`, always set `sizes`. Set `priority`/`loading="eager"`
  on the above-the-fold image (first grid row); leave the rest on default lazy
  loading.

## Filtering / query shape

- If a column has an index (e.g. `instructor_slug`/`style`/`level` in
  `migrations/0009_catalog_indexes.sql`), push `WHERE`-able filters down into
  the SQL query. Don't fetch the whole table and `Array.filter()` in JS —
  that pays the full fetch/join cost on every filtered request and leaves the
  index unused.
- Any non-`next/image` asset (raw `<img>`, `<video poster>`, etc.) still needs
  explicit `width`/`height` to avoid layout shift, since nothing resizes it
  at runtime either.

## Client bundle

- Don't let a client SDK only needed for signed-in flows (e.g. `firebase/auth`)
  load unconditionally on pages anonymous visitors hit most (home, catalog
  browsing). Lazy-init it, or gate it behind the auth-related UI that actually
  needs it.

## Static asset caching

- `public/_headers`'s long-cache rule only covers `/_next/static/*` (content-hashed).
  Anything else served straight from `public/` (posters, avatars, logo) needs
  its own explicit `Cache-Control` rule there too — it won't get one by default.

## When adding/expanding mock or seed data at scale

Before considering a data-scaling task (like growing a catalog) done, sanity-check
the read paths against the new row count: re-run the affected pages/API routes and
watch for multi-second responses or multi-MB payloads — issues invisible at 3 rows
become severe at 100+.
